     But[0m[2m wait[0m[2m: what[0m[2m if the[0m[2m same order[0m[2m_id is[0m[2m called concurrently[0m[2m? Both[0m[2m do[0m[2m sleep,[0m[2m then both[0m[2m evaluate[0m[2m random ([0m[2mmaybe[0m[2m both pass[0m[2m), then[0m[2m both try[0m[2m to acquire[0m[2m lock.[0m[2m One[0m[2m gets in[0m[2m first[0m[2m, adds[0m[2m to set[0m[2m, app[0m[2mends,[0m[2m returns[0m[2m True.[0m[2m The second[0m[2m gets[0m[2m in,[0m[2m sees order[0m[2m_id in[0m[2m set,[0m[2m returns True[0m[2m. That[0m[2m is id[0m[2mempotent.[0m[2m No[0m[2m duplicate charge[0m[2m record[0m[2m. Good[0m[2m.
     
     What[0m[2m about[0m[2m total[0m[2m_ch[0m[2marged?[0m[2m Since the[0m[2m append[0m[2m and addition[0m[2m are under[0m[2m the lock[0m[2m, it's[0m[2m safe[0m[2m.
     
     But[0m[2m is[0m[2m float[0m[2m += atomic[0m[2m enough[0m[2m? Under[0m[2m lock[0m[2m it's[0m[2m definitely[0m[2m safe[0m[2m.[0m[2m Even[0m[2m without lock[0m[2m, in[0m[2m single[0m[2m-threaded[0m[2m asyncio it's[0m[2m atomic,[0m[2m but using[0m[2m lock is[0m[2m cleaner[0m[2m.
     
     What[0m[2m if[0m[2m we[0m[2m want to[0m[2m allow the[0m[2m same[0m[2m order_id[0m[2m to be[0m[2m retried[0m[2m after a[0m[2m failure?[0m[2m The prompt[0m[2m says "[0m[2mNo order[0m[2m is charged[0m[2m more than[0m[2m once."[0m[2m So[0m[2m if a[0m[2m charge fails[0m[2m, should[0m[2m it[0m[2m be ret[0m[2mried?[0m[2m It[0m[2m says[0m[2m "no[0m[2m order is[0m[2m charged more[0m[2m than once[0m[2m", meaning[0m[2m if it[0m[2m eventually[0m[2m succeeds,[0m[2m only[0m[2m once.[0m[2m But if[0m[2m it[0m[2m fails,[0m[2m maybe[0m[2m it[0m[2m shouldn't be[0m[2m charged[0m[2m later[0m[2m either[0m[2m? Usually[0m[2m if[0m[2m a payment[0m[2m fails,[0m[2m you can[0m[2m retry.[0m[2m But the[0m[2m requirement is[0m[2m ambiguous.[0m[2m However,[0m[2m in[0m[2m our[0m[2m checkout[0m[2m flow[0m[2m, we[0m[2m only call[0m[2m charge once[0m[2m.[0m[2m The[0m[2m duplicate[0m[2m charge guard[0m[2m is for[0m[2m safety[0m[2m.[0m[2m
     
     I[0m[2m think the[0m[2m simplest is[0m[2m: if[0m[2m already[0m[2m charged ([0m[2msuccessfully[0m[2m), return[0m[2m True.[0m[2m If not[0m[2m,[0m[2m proceed[0m[2m with[0m[2m random[0m[2m failure[0m[2m check[0m[2m and then[0m[2m record under[0m[2m lock.[0m[2m If[0m[2m it[0m[2m fails random[0m[2m check[0m[2m, we[0m[2m don't add[0m[2m to set[0m[2m.[0m[2m So a[0m[2m future[0m[2m retry could[0m[2m succeed[0m[2m. But[0m[2m if[0m[2m we[0m[2m want[0m[2m to prevent[0m[2m any[0m[2m retry[0m[2m after[0m[2m a[0m[2m successful[0m[2m charge,[0m[2m the[0m[2m set tracks[0m[2m successful[0m[2m charges[0m[2m.[0m[2m That's fine[0m[2m.
     
